        "excerpt": "Technical notes on hypermedia & flat-file CMS.",
        "tags": [],
        "reads": 1852,
        "created_at": "2026-07-10T10:00:00",
        "updated_at": "2026-07-10T10:00:00",
        "body": "<section class='mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14'> <h1 class='text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900'>Blog</h1> <p class='mt-2 text-slate-500'>Notes on hypermedia, Datastar, SSE, and flat-file CMS design.</p> <div class='mt-8 space-y-4'> {% for a in collection('posts', {sort:'-created_at'}) %} <a href='{{ a.url }}' class='block rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-indigo-300'> <div class='text-xs text-slate-400'>{{ a.created_at|fdate('d M Y') }}</div> <div class='mt-1 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900'>{{ a.title }}</div> <p class='mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500'>{{ a.excerpt }}</p> <div class='mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2'>{% for t in a.tags %}<span class='rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-slate-600'>#{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}</div> </a> {% endfor %} </div> </section>"
    },
    {
        "id": "pg_produk",
        "type": "page",
        "title": "Products",
        "slug": "products",
        "layout": "full",
        "status": "published",
        "excerpt": "Sample product catalog.",
        "tags": [],
        "reads": 2446,
        "created_at": "2026-07-11T10:00:00",
        "updated_at": "2026-07-11T10:00:00",
        "body": "<section class='mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14'> <h1 class='text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900'>Products</h1> <p class='mt-2 text-slate-500'>Every price &amp; stock value is read straight from a JSON record.</p> <div class='mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3'> {% for p in collection('products') %} <a href='{{ p.url }}' class='rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-sm'> <div class='text-3xl'>{{ p.attrs.emoji|default('📦') }}</div> <div class='mt-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400'>{{ p.attrs.category }}</div> <div class='font-semibold text-slate-900'>{{ p.title }}</div> <p class='mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500'>{{ p.excerpt }}</p> <div class='mt-2 font-semibold text-slate-900'>{{ p.attrs.price|money }}</div> <div class='text-xs {% if p.attrs.stock > 0 %}text-emerald-600{% else %}text-rose-500{% endif %}'>{% if p.attrs.stock > 0 %}{{ p.attrs.stock }} in stock{% else %}Sold out{% endif %}</div> </a> {% endfor %} </div> </section>"
    },
    {
        "id": "pg_tentang",
        "type": "page",
        "title": "About",
        "slug": "about",
        "layout": "article",
        "status": "published",
        "excerpt": "What NoBuildCMS is.",
        "tags": [],
        "reads": 669,
        "created_at": "2026-07-17T10:00:00",
        "updated_at": "2026-07-17T10:00:00",
        "body": "<section class='mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14'> <h1 class='text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900'>About</h1> <p class='mt-4 text-slate-600'>NoBuildCMS is a mini CMS &amp; hypermedia dashboard. The backend is native PHP, templates are sandboxed Twig, reactivity is powered by Datastar, and data is stored as JSON files — no database, no build step.</p> <p class='mt-4 text-slate-600'>Every change in the dashboard shows up on the public site in real time over SSE. Content is a Twig template that can query other collections, datasets, and snippets.</p> <h2 class='mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900'>Team</h2> <p class='mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500'>Rendered from data('team')</p> <div class='mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3'> {% for m in data('team') %} <div class='rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5'><div class='font-semibold text-slate-900'>{{ m.name }}</div><div class='text-sm text-slate-500'>{{ m.role }}</div></div> {% endfor %} </div> <div class='mt-10'>{{ snippet('cta') }}</div> </section>"
    },
    {
        "id": "pg_kontak",
        "type": "page",
        "title": "Contact",
        "slug": "contact",
